# YHWH Bible publishing platform — environment variables (ξ.6).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (already in .gitignore) and fill in
# values. Cross-reference: `dev/SECURITY.md` §4 for the canonical
# documentation; this file is the example/skeleton template.
#
# Naming convention: project-prefixed variables use `YHWH_*` for
# config / `EBIBLE_*` for legacy auth. Apple-specific signing vars
# follow the platform's standard names (CODESIGN_*, NOTARIZE_*).
#
# All variables are READ via `os.environ.get(...)` — none are
# required at process startup. Missing values produce specific
# errors at the call site that needs them.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Content + paths
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Override the default `content/` root. Useful for tests + multi-
# checkout dev workflows. Tests prefer `paths.set_content_root_for_testing()`
# in-process; this env var is for ad-hoc CLI use.
# YHWH_CONTENT_ROOT=/path/to/alternate/content

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (web)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Admin token gating `/api/*` mutation endpoints. Required only when
# the launcher runs with `--auth-token`. Omit for single-user
# localhost mode (the default) — auth checks pass open.
# EBIBLE_ADMIN_TOKEN=replace-me-with-a-long-random-string

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# EPUB validation
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Path to IDPF `epubcheck.jar` for build-time EPUB validation. Java
# runtime must be on PATH. Defaults to a project-relative path; set
# this only if your install lives elsewhere.
# EPUBCHECK_JAR=/usr/local/lib/epubcheck/epubcheck.jar

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI detectors (χ-AI-xrefs / χ-AI-notes — opt-in, paid)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Anthropic API key for the AI cross-reference and note detectors.
# Read at call time only; omit if you don't run the paid detectors.
# Future ξ.14 phase moves this to OS keychain (macOS Keychain /
# Windows Credential Manager / Linux Secret Service).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Desktop binary signing (θ.4 — opt-in, requires paid certs)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# macOS code-signing identity. Look up via `security find-identity
# -v -p codesigning` after installing the Apple Developer ID cert
# in your login keychain.
# CODESIGN_IDENTITY=Developer ID Application: Your Name (XXXXXXXXXX)

# Apple Developer Team ID. Found in your Apple Developer account
# under Membership.
# TEAMID=XXXXXXXXXX

# Notarization keychain profile name (created via `xcrun notarytool
# store-credentials`). Used by θ.4 macOS signing scripts.
# NOTARIZE_KEYCHAIN_PROFILE=yhwh-notary

# Apple Connect profile alias used by θ.4 macOS notarization.
# AC_PROFILE=yhwh-ac
